# comfyui.schema — who may set each key of the `comfyui` subsystem (see w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# Every key is `system`. ComfyUI runs on W as ONE machine-wide service under its
# own account — the analogue of ollama.service, not a per-account app: where it
# is installed, which address it answers on, which PyTorch build sits in its
# virtualenv and what its command line says are all root-domain facts, and a user
# layer could not act on them anyway (the unit is rendered by a root setup step).
# A fleet that wants to fix them harder still can: policy.d sits above the admin
# layer and locks the keys.
ROOT	system
LISTEN	system
PORT	system
GPU	system
ARGS	system
